SQL: To find clusters of schools lacking facilities, we will identify schools missing essential infrastructure and group them by their respective clusters. Here's the query:


SELECT
  c."cluster_name",
  ST_Centroid(c.geometry) AS centroid,
  COUNT(*) as school_count
FROM
  meghalaya_schools s
JOIN
  meghalaya_infrastructure i ON s."udiseCode" = i.udise_code
JOIN
  meghalaya_district_intelligence_final d ON d.district_name = s.district_name
JOIN
  meghalaya_block_intelligence_final b ON b.district_name = s.district_name AND ST_Within(b.geometry, s.geometry)
JOIN
  (
    SELECT
      c."cluster_name",
      i.*
    FROM
      meghalaya_schools s
    JOIN
      meghalaya_infrastructure i ON s."udiseCode" = i.udise_code
    WHERE
      NOT (
        i.electricity_connection_available = 1 OR
        i.playground_available = 1 OR
        i.ramp_available = 1 OR
        i.drinking_water_availability = 1 OR
        i.solar_panel = 1
      )
  ) c ON ST_Within(c.geometry, b.geometry)
GROUP BY
  c."cluster_name",
  centroid
ORDER BY
  school_count DESC;


This query will find clusters of schools lacking essential infrastructure (electricity, playground, ramp, drinking water, or solar panel) and sort them by the number of such schools in descending order.;


